bility":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.022431826295691293,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":22.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01572206074932149,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":73.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.02545,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":17.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alignment Healthcare, Inc. operates a consumer-centric healthcare platform for seniors in the United States. It delivers customized healthcare experience to meet the needs of seniors through its Medicare Advantage plans. Alignment Healthcare, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is based in Orange, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John E. Kao | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $2.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 36%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $61K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Alignment Healthcare, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.5B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +40% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","The business throws off $113M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -13.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $26.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Alignment Healthcare (ALHC) & Its Rivals","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/contrasting-alignment-healthcare-alhc-its-rivals.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970923.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (ALHC) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_ALHC_Edition_110526063202_1793878322.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793878322.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alignment Healthcare (NASDAQ:ALHC) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from TD Cowen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/alignment-healthcare-nasdaqalhc-stock-gets-price-target-trim-from-td-cowen.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793859893.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Is Alignment Healthcare (ALHC) Undervalued After Raised Guidance And A Quarterly Loss?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.